SUMMARY:Epic Day on Cold Mountain 10.5 Miles - Fitness Hike
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**DISTANCE** 10.5 mile out and Bac
 k\n\n**ELEVATION GAIN:** Approximately 2\,900 feet Level 9\\* hike.\n\n**H
 IKE DESCRIPTION:** **Cold Mountain via the Art Loeb Trail is one the most 
 iconic hikes in western North Carolina.** The Art Loeb Trail goes left fro
 m the parking area of the Scout camp\, ascending a rugged 3.8 miles to Dee
 p Gap\, gaining about 1800 ft.\, and entering the demanding high country o
 f the Shining Rock Wilderness Area. At Deep Gap we'll go left to continue 
 a 1.5 mile final summit assault. There are expansive views from several ro
 ck outcrop overlooks @ 6\,000 elevation\, at or near the top. Higher eleva
 tion hike will have cooler temperatures. Make sure to bring rain/cold weat
 her gear. This hike is mostly under a hardwood forest. In exchange for the
  effort\, on a clear day\, you're rewarded with sweeping views\, high elev
 ation balds and long stretches of open ridgelines that showcase the best o
 f the Blue Ridge Mountains. Come prepared for an epic day!\n\n**PACE:** We
  hike at a brisk pace average 2.5-3 MPH adjusting for rugged and/or steep 
 trail conditions with brief regroup as needed. We will have lunch at the t
 op to enjoy the vistas across layered mountain ranges. We return on the sa
 me trail\, which will be mostly a downhill course through thin forest\, de
 scending into rhododendron tunnels. This hike is for conditioned hikers.\n
 \n**CARPOOL:** Meet at the Cracker Barrel in West Asheville at 8:10am. If 
 you plan to carpool\, please let us know in the comments section.\n\n**TEM
 PERATURE** is usually 10-15 degrees colder than Asheville and can be breez
 y at the top. The beginning of the trail is rocky and usually damp or with
  wet sections. This is a popular\, well-traveled trail.\n\n**WEATHER:** We
  will cancel this hike\, or change to another\, on or before 7:00am on hik
 e day if the weather conditions are not favorable.\n\n**DOGS** are welcome
 \, but make sure you bring a leash. Driving time to the trailhead is about
  45 minutes.\n\n**HIKE LEVEL:** level 9 (of 10) hikes have an elevation ga
 in between 2\,700 and 2\,999 feet. Estimated elevation gain for this hike 
 is about 2\,900 feet.\n\n**DIRECTIONS** to trailhead: Take I-40 West to ex
 it 37. Turn left and then right onto Smokey Park Highway (US Hwy 23) at th
 e Exxon station. Follow Hwy. 23 south through downtown and turn left onto 
 NC Highway 110. Go 5.3 miles\, and Highway 110 will turn into NC Highway 2
 15. Continue for 5 miles. Turn left onto Little East Fork Road. Go 3.8 mil
 es to the Scout Camp. Go past several buildings and the ART LOEB/ Cold Mou
 ntain trailhead is on the left.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315646929
 /
