SUMMARY:Jones Gap and Rainbow Falls
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nJones Gap and Rainbow Falls - appr
 ox 6 miles with 1\,000' of elevation gain.\nLength: 6 miles\nElevation Gai
 n: 1\,000'\nSpeed: 2-2.5 mph average\nDifficultly: moderate\n\nOK\, 6 mile
 s is a pretty short hike but the climb up to Rainbow Falls makes it more i
 nteresting.\n\nWe'll start from the Jones Gap State Park entrance and hike
  about 1.5 miles over to Jones Gap Falls. From Jones Gap Falls we'll start
  back towards the park entrance and intersect with the Rainbow Falls trail
 . Here we'll climb close to 1\,000' in 1.5 miles to Rainbow Falls then ret
 urn to the cars.\n\nThere is a $6.00 per person admission to Jones Gap Sta
 te Park unless you have a SC State Park parking pass.\n\nAnyone wanting to
  car pool can meet at the Cracker Barrell on Upward Rd off of I-26 for a 9
 :30 departure. Hike starts at 10.\n\nDogs are welcome\, I will have my dog
  with me.
